      "title": "Teach our console log handler to use log domains (Unix)",
      "message": "Teach our console log handler to use log domains (Unix)\n\nBy punting to the default log handler. tshark is using\ng_log_default_handler(), Qt is too. Is there a reason\nWireshark cannot do the same?\n\nUsing g_defaut_log_handler() allows the user to\nselectively turn on INFO and DEBUG messages using\nthe environment variable G_MESSAGES_DEBUG.\n\nThe fact that the output format is now consistent with\ntshark is also a nice bonus.\n\nPing #17271.\n",
      "author_name": "João Valverde",
      "author_email": "joao.valverde@tecnico.ulisboa.pt",
      "authored_date": "2021-03-05T03:34:51.000+00:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-03-06T12:40:20.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/b5530e7021fa68c1d8e7e454b758cfea64acd6ba"
    },
    {
